INT. ORBITAL ELEVATOR CAR - MID-ASCENT - NIGHT

A glass-walled cylinder rising through darkness. Below, the curve of a blue-black Earth. The car hums. A status panel reads 22,000 KM AND CLIMBING.

Six passengers share the car. MARGUERITE OSEI (50s, mission commander, grey crop) grips the handrail. TOMAS VELASCO (30s, pilot, flight suit) leans on the wall. DR. HANA IWASAKI (40s, biologist) holds a sealed specimen case. NAVIN BHATT (20s, engineer, thick gloves) kneels at an access panel. COLLIN FAIRWEATHER (60s, corporate observer, tie loosened) sits on the floor. And ROSALIND "ROZ" TEAGUE (30s, medic) checks a handheld.

The car shudders. All six stop talking.

OSEI
What was that?

NAVIN
Tether tension.

TOMAS
That's not tension, that's a stutter.

HANA
Is the case secure?

ROZ
It's secure. Is Collin secure?

COLLIN
I'm fine.

ROZ
You're sweating.

COLLIN
It's warm.

OSEI
It's minus ten.

The panel flickers. The ascent counter drops a number, then climbs again. Navin's head jerks up from the access panel.

NAVIN
We slipped.

OSEI
We what?

NAVIN
Forty metres. We dropped forty metres.

TOMAS
Commander, I'm reading a cable fault on the line.

HANA
How bad?

TOMAS
Bad enough to ask.

OSEI
Navin, can you reach the manual brake?

NAVIN
If someone holds the lamp.

COLLIN
I'll hold it.

ROZ
You will not. Hana.

HANA
Me?

ROZ
You've got the steadiest hands.

Hana sets the case on the seat and picks up the lamp. Her hand does shake. She sees it and steadies it with the other. Navin pulls a lever. The brake groans. The car jolts and holds.

TOMAS
We're locked.

OSEI
Everyone breathe.

They do. For a moment, only the sound of six people inhaling. Then the panel chimes: FAULT ISOLATED. HOLD POSITION.

OSEI
Tomas, confirm.

TOMAS
Confirmed. We're not going anywhere.

Osei lets go of the rail. Her fingers have gone white. She looks around the car at each of them in turn: Tomas calm, Hana trembling, Navin sweating, Collin ashen, Roz watching Collin.

ROZ
(low, to Osei)
He knows something.

OSEI
(low)
I know he does.

Collin looks away.
